Stop the heartbeat paths writing to an engine that has hit an I/O error

When a stream engine's inbound pipe is full (the application is not
draining the socket as fast as one peer sends), it stops polling for input
and waits for the session to call restart_input ().  If the connection dies
in that window the poller still delivers EPOLLERR/EPOLLHUP as in_event (),
which removes the fd and sets _io_error, but deliberately keeps the engine
alive so that restart_input () can deliver what was already decoded before
tearing it down.  That state is absorbing: the flag is never cleared, and
every exit from it destroys the engine.

Two things can still try to write through that dead engine, and both land in
out_event (), which asserts !_io_error and aborts the process:

  - the heartbeat interval timer, which keeps firing since only unplug ()
    cancels it: "Assertion failed: !_io_error (src/stream_engine_base.cpp:331)"
    from timer_event ();

  - a PING decoded during restart_input (), whose PONG reply goes straight
    to out_event () (upstream issue #4364).

Cancel the interval timer at the point the engine enters that state, and
skip the PONG when the connection is already gone.  This keeps the
out_event () invariant intact rather than relaxing the assertion, which
upstream rejected in PR #4852.  Reported upstream as #4841/#4842; present in
every release through 4.3.5 and in master.

--- a/src/stream_engine_base.hpp
+++ b/src/stream_engine_base.hpp
@@ -175,8 +175,13 @@

     msg_t _tx_msg;

+  protected:
+    //  Set once the connection is gone while input was stopped; the engine
+    //  then only waits for restart_input () to deliver what it already
+    //  decoded before erroring out, and nothing may be written any more.
     bool _io_error;

+  private:
     //  The session this engine is attached to.
     zmq::session_base_t *_session;

--- a/src/stream_engine_base.cpp
+++ b/src/stream_engine_base.cpp
@@ -247,6 +247,16 @@
     if (_input_stopped) {
         rm_fd (_handle);
         _io_error = true;
+
+        //  The engine now lives on only until restart_input () has pushed
+        //  what is already decoded into the pipe, after which it errors out.
+        //  Nothing can be written in the meantime, so the heartbeat interval
+        //  timer must not fire: its out_event () call would trip the
+        //  !_io_error assertion.
+        if (_has_heartbeat_timer) {
+            cancel_timer (heartbeat_ivl_timer_id);
+            _has_heartbeat_timer = false;
+        }
         return true; // TODO or return false in this case too?
     }

--- a/src/zmtp_engine.cpp
+++ b/src/zmtp_engine.cpp
@@ -522,9 +522,15 @@
                     static_cast<uint8_t *> (msg_->data ()) + ping_ttl_len,
                     context_len);

-        _next_msg = static_cast<int (stream_engine_base_t::*) (msg_t *)> (
-          &zmtp_engine_t::produce_pong_message);
-        out_event ();
+        //  A PING can still be decoded from restart_input () after the
+        //  connection is already gone (_io_error set while input was
+        //  stopped); the reply cannot be sent, and out_event () must not be
+        //  entered in that state.
+        if (!_io_error) {
+            _next_msg = static_cast<int (stream_engine_base_t::*) (msg_t *)> (
+              &zmtp_engine_t::produce_pong_message);
+            out_event ();
+        }
     }

     return 0;
